  "final_answer": "I have all the storage options and prices for both iPad Pro models. Here is the complete information:\n\n## iPad Pro (M5 chip) Storage Options and Prices\n\nApple's website offers the latest iPad Pro in two sizes with four storage configurations each:\n\n### 11-inch iPad Pro\n| Storage | Memory | Chip | Price |\n|---------|--------|------|-------|\n| 256GB | 12GB | M5 (9-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,199 |\n| 512GB | 12GB | M5 (9-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,399 |\n| 1TB | 16GB | M5 (10-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,799 |\n| 2TB | 16GB | M5 (10-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $2,299 |\n\n### 13-inch iPad Pro\n| Storage | Memory | Chip | Price |\n|---------|--------|------|-------|\n| 256GB | 12GB | M5 (9-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,499 |\n| 512GB | 12GB | M5 (9-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,699 |\n| 1TB | 16GB | M5 (10-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $2,099 |\n| 2TB | 16GB | M5 (10-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $2,599 |\n\n**Key observations:**\n- Both sizes are available in two colors: Space Black and Silver.\n- Higher storage tiers (1TB/2TB) come with more memory (16GB vs 12GB) and a more powerful M5 chip variant (10-core CPU vs 9-core CPU).\n- The 13-inch model costs $300 more than the equivalent 11-inch model at every storage tier.\n- Monthly payment options start at $99.91/mo. (11-inch/256GB) up to $216.58/mo. (13-inch/2TB), with Apple Upgrade Program lease options as low as $24.99/mo.",
